From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] composefs: export the booted image with uncompressed layers

`bootc image copy-to-storage` writes the booted image as an OCI layout in
/var/tmp and has skopeo copy it into containers-storage, which keeps layers
uncompressed. The layout was gzipped on one thread only for skopeo to
decompress it again, which made copying a multi-gigabyte image take minutes.
Write its layers uncompressed: the tar streams, their diff ids and so the
image's config and ID stay as they were.
---
diff --git a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/export.rs b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/export.rs
index 745519a..2e14abc 100644
--- a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/export.rs
+++ b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/export.rs
@@ -79,7 +79,11 @@ pub async fn export_repo_to_image(
 
         let mut layer_stream = booted_cfs.repo.open_stream("", Some(layer_verity), None)?;
 
-        let mut layer_writer = oci_dir.create_layer(None)?;
+        // Uncompressed: this layout is only scratch on its way into
+        // containers-storage, which stores layers uncompressed. Compressing
+        // the whole image with single-threaded gzip only for skopeo to
+        // decompress it again cost the self-install minutes.
+        let mut layer_writer = tar::Builder::new(oci_dir.create_uncompressed_layer()?);
         layer_writer.follow_symlinks(false);
 
         let mut got_zero_block = false;
